.IP "\fBXmNdialogType\fP" 8
Specifies the type of the dialog (\fIXmDIALOG_FONT\fP).
.IP "\fBXmNsource\fP" 8
Specifies whether to load Xft (\fIXmFONT_SOURCE_XFT\fP) or
X (\fIXmFONT_SOURCE_X\fP) fonts.
.IP "\fBXmNprefer100dpi\fP" 8
If \fBTrue\fP ignore 75 dpi fonts. Only applicable for X fonts.
.IP "\fBXmNvisibleItemCount\fP" 8
Number of items to keep visible in each of the three lists.
.IP "\fBXmNfontString\fP" 8
String to display above the font list.
.IP "\fBXmNstyleString\fP" 8
String to display above the style list.
.IP "\fBXmNsizeString\fP" 8
String to display above the size list.
.IP "\fBXmNsampleTitle\fP" 8
Title for the sample frame.
.IP "\fBXmNsampleText\fP" 8
Sample text to render in the frame.
.IP "\fBXmNokLabelString\fP" 8
Label for the \fBOK\fP button. If unspecified, this uses the localized
version of "OK" provided by \fBXmBulletinBoard\fP.
.IP "\fBXmNcancelLabelString\fP" 8
Label for the \fBCancel\fP button. If unspecified, this uses the localized
version of "Cancel" provided by \fBXmBulletinBoard\fP.
.IP "\fBXmNokCallback\fP" 8
Callback list for \fBXmNactivate\fP on the \fBOK\fP button.
.IP "\fBXmNcancelCallback\fP" 8
Callback list for \fBXmNactivate\fP on the \fBCancel\fP button.

.SS INHERITED RESOURCES
See \fBXmBulletinBoard\fP(3).

.SH CALLBACKS
A pointer to the following structure is passed to each callback routine
for \fBXmNokCallback\fP and \fBXmNcancelCallback\fP:

.nf
typedef struct {
	\fBint \fPreason;
	\fBXEvent *\fPevent;
	\fBXmRendition \fPrendition;
} XmFontDialogCallbackStruct;
.fi
.IP "\fIreason\fP" 10
Indicates why the callback was invoked (\fBXmCR_OK\fP or \fBXmCR_CANCEL\fP)
.IP "\fIevent\fP" 10
The \fBXEvent\fP that triggered the callback
.IP "\fIrendition\fP" 10
A copy of the currently selected rendition, supplied to the \fBOK\fP
callback. The callback must free this.

